when i can't sleep nights i come up with strange ideas ...

it is arguably too unbalancing for a player to have intrinsic identify.
how about a special form of identify (to be called thaumaturgy?) that
a wizard has intrinsically and others can get if their combined wisdom
and intelligence equals or exceeds, lets say 36?  thaumaturgy would
enable the possessor to #guess the instances of "rustproof" or "charged"
and other obscure properties of objects (but not blessings).  occasionally
you might also get a number for unidentified objects but this is magically
complicated:  for objects which can have +/- enchantment you would only
get an enigmatic positive number (this assumes you don't know the blessed
state) and for other objects like wands that usually have plus charges
you would also get a positive number but the #guess itself would decrease
the number of charges (usually by one).  successive guesses on an unknown
wand would eventually deplete all the charges (possibly causing an
explosion).  this might not work too well since some wands are
characterized by their charges ...

using thaumaturgy on a plumed hat might yield:
#guess   m - plumed hat

2
waterproof

meaning that the hat has either +2 or -2 enchantment and is waterproof
(probably leather).

is this strange or what???

